<title>FRANCE: Valeo aims for 97 sales above 32 bln.</title>
<headline>Valeo aims for 97 sales above 32 bln.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French car parts manufacturer Valeo said on Wednesday it is seeking sales of more than 32 billion francs in 1997, after sales of 28.87 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>On May 21, the company had forecast 1997 sales of more than 30 billion francs.</p>
<p>&quot;In a European car market which should be more active in the second half and assuming a U.S. market which is slowing down, but still at a high level, Valeo has fixed a target of showing turnover above 32 billion francs in 1997,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
</text>
